          %title Seiberg-Witten curve
          %h3#ReferencesSeibergWittenCurve Seiberg-Witten curve
          %h4#swcurve_in_swtheory SW-curve in SW-theory
          %p
            The notion of the
            %em Seiberg-Witten curve
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seiberg-Witten+theory"} Seiberg-Witten theory
            originates in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"}> Nathan Seiberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              %em
                Monopoles, duality and chiral symmetry breaking in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=2
              %p
                supersymmetric QCD, Nucl. Phys. B431 (1994) 484-550 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9408099"}> hep-th/9408099
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taro+Kimura"}> Taro Kimura
              , §4.2.3.1 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Instanton Counting, Quantum Geometry and Algebra
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-76190-5_4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-030-76190-5_4
          %p
            and in relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+systems"} integrable systems
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Marshakov"}> Andrei Marshakov
              ,
              %em Seiberg-Witten Curves and Integrable Systems
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9903252"}> arXiv:hep-th/9903252
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h4#ReferencesSWCurveAsM5Worldvolume As M5-brane worldvolume
          %p
            Observation that under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometric engineering
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D4+N%3D2+SYM"} D=4 N=2 SYM
            on
            %a{:href => "NS5-brane#D4EndingOnNS5"} D4/NS5 intersections
            and further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} lift
            to a single
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            transverse to the SYM-spacetime:
          %ul
            %li#KlemmLercheMayrVafaWarner96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albrecht+Klemm"}> Albrecht Klemm
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Lerche"} Wolfgang Lerche
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Mayr"} Peter Mayr
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Warner"} Nicholas Warner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Self-Dual Strings and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒩
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=2
                    Supersymmetric Field Theory
                %strong 477
                (1996) 746-766 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9604034"}> arXiv:hep-th/9604034
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(96)00353-7"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(96)00353-7
            %li#Witten97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Solutions Of Four-Dimensional Field Theories Via M Theory
                %strong 500
                (1997) 3-42 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9703166"}> arXiv:hep-th/9703166
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00416-1"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00416-1
          %p Further early discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Karl Landsteiner, Esperanza Lopez, David A. Lowe,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒩
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
                    \=2 Supersymmetric Gauge Theories, Branes and Orientifolds
                %strong 507
                (1997) 197-226 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9705199"}> arXiv:hep-th/9705199
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00559-2"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00559-2
            %li
              %p
                A. Brandhuber,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Sonnenschein"} Jacob Sonnenschein
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Theisen"} Stefan Theisen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shimon+Yankielowicz"} Shimon Yankielowicz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em M Theory And Seiberg-Witten Curves: Orthogonal and Symplectic Groups
                %strong 504
                (1997) 175-188 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9705232"}> arXiv:hep-th/9705232
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00531-2"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(97)00531-2
          %p Review in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Csaba Csaki, Joshua Erlich, John Terning, pp. 4 of;
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Seiberg-Witten Description of the Deconstructed 6D
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,2)
                    Theory
                %strong 67
                025019 (2003) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0208095"}> arXiv:hep-th/0208095
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.67.025019"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.67.025019
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francesco+Benini"}> Francesco Benini
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergio+Benvenuti"} Sergio Benvenuti
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuji+Tachikawa"} Yuji Tachikawa
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Webs of five-branes and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒩
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=2
                    superconformal field theories
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0906.0359"} arXiv:0906.0359
            %li
              %p
                Ling Bao, Elli Pomoni, Masato Taki, Futoshi Yagi, p. 5 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em M5-branes, toric diagrams and gauge theory duality
                %strong 2012
                105 (2012) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1112.5228"}> arXiv:1112.5228
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP04(2012)105"} doi:10.1007/JHEP04(2012)105
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taro+Kimura"}> Taro Kimura
                , §4.5.2 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Seiberg–Witten Geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Instanton Counting, Quantum Geometry and Algebra
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-76190-5_4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-030-76190-5_4
          %h4#quantum_swcurve Quantum SW-curve
          %p
            On the “quantum SW curve”, a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantized
            SW curve:
          %ul
            %li
              Alba Grassi, Jie Gu,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcos+Mari%C3%B1o"} Marcos Mariño
              = succeed "," do
                %em Non-perturbative approaches to the quantum Seiberg-Witten curve
              %strong 2020
              106 (2020) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07065"}> arXiv:1908.07065
              ,
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP07(2020)106"} doi:10.1007/JHEP07(2020)106
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            In relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+S-theories"} class S-theories
            and “
